Chapter Four: Accidents  
144.* (a) The driver of a vehicle involved in an accident resulting in the death or injury of a person shall act according to the following instructions:  
(1) He shall immediately stop the vehicle at the scene of the accident or as close as possible to it, and shall not move it from its place unless it is necessary to use the vehicle for the purpose of performing the actions specified in paragraph (2) or if a police officer has permitted it;  
(2) Depending on the circumstances of the case and the location of the accident, he shall provide appropriate assistance to any person injured in that accident, and in particular –  
(a) Ensure the prevention of any further harm to the injured;  
(b) Provide first aid that he is capable of providing according to his training;  
(c) Call for the necessary professional rescue services to the scene of the accident according to the circumstances of the case, including an ambulance, police, and fire services;  
(d) Wait by the injured person until the professional rescue services arrive;  
(e) In a situation where it is not possible to transport the injured by ambulance, he shall ensure their transfer by another suitable vehicle to a first aid station, hospital, or doctor.  
(3) He shall provide to a police officer, or to a person who was injured or to the driver of another vehicle involved in the same accident, or to any passenger or person who was with the injured, his name and address, his driver's license number and the registration number of the vehicle he is driving, and the name and address of its owner, and shall present upon their request his driver's license, vehicle license, or insurance certificate and...

