Street Vegetation
The selection of street vegetation is made - in addition to architectural/aesthetic considerations - based on several factors:
- Water conservation - drought-resistant plants with low water consumption are preferred;
- Conflict resolution with infrastructure (power lines, signage and lighting, various types of piping, and sidewalks);
- Maintenance - pruning and cleaning of the sidewalk;
- Climatic benefits - for example, choosing trees also considering the size of the tree's canopy;
- Growth rate;
- Diversity of plant species and vegetation capable of supporting as rich a variety of species as possible;
- Consideration of the allergenic potential of the vegetation.

